description:
Loads published daily mean temperature and daily mean dewpoint collections over a time range, computes relative humidity from them with earthkit-meteo's `relative_humidity_from_dewpoint`, and publishes the result as a new GeoZarr dataset.

Relative humidity computed from daily means is an estimate of the daily mean of hourly relative humidity. Saturation vapour pressure is exponential in temperature, so it runs slightly low, most where the diurnal temperature range is large. Checked against ERA5-Land's hourly-based `era5land_relative_humidity_daily` on single days in Niamey, Nairobi and around Lake Victoria, it was within about 0.1 to 1.6 percentage points, closer than the FAO-56 estimates from daily minimum and maximum temperature. Use it where only daily inputs exist; where hourly inputs exist, prefer an hourly-based dataset.

For ERA5-Land, the inputs are `era5land_temperature_daily` and `era5land_dewpoint_daily`. The two inputs must share a grid and time axis. Their units are converted to Kelvin from the units their data sources declare, and the result is in '%'.

If the output dataset has no registered data source, OCS auto-registers one from the dewpoint dataset's metadata. Keep the dataset current by re-running the workflow over the new range after its inputs sync.

Zarr output cannot be produced synchronously, so run this as a batch job (`POST /jobs`, then `POST /jobs/{id}/results`):

{
  "rh": {
    "process_id": "relative_humidity_from_daily_dewpoint",
    "arguments": {
      "temperature_dataset_id": "era5land_temperature_daily",
      "dewpoint_dataset_id": "era5land_dewpoint_daily",
      "output_dataset_id": "era5land_relative_humidity_daily_estimated",
      "variable": "rh",
      "temporal_extent": ["2024-01-01", "2024-12-31"]
    },
    "result": true
  }
}
